Sval: pass the painted frame to the colors that skip nsIFrame

Borders, outlines, backgrounds, gradient stops, SVG fill and stroke and
collapsed table borders resolve their colors from a ComputedStyle, which
knows no frame, so they would keep the page's colors under a site style.
Each passes the frame it paints. A text field's background is a theme
color no style resolves, and a background-color animation runs on the
compositor, so both take the style where their color is made, as do a
button's and a select's themed faces. A link's border is resolved
without its frame, since it is styled where it is drawn.

